  <static seed="151" source="Library/UCSB/Stewart5_2_6/Stewart5_2_6_54.pg">
    <statement><p>A tank contains <m>5000</m> L of pure water. Brine that contains <m>30</m> g of salt per liter of water is pumped into the tank at a rate of <m>25</m> L/min. The concentration of salt after <m>t</m> minutes can be shown to be given by:</p>
<p><me>C(t)=\displaystyle \frac{30t}{200+t}</me></p>
<p>What happens to the concentration as <m>t \to \infty</m>?</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle \lim_{ t \to \infty} C(t)=</m> <fillin characters="10" name="AnSwEr0001"/> g/L</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>30</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
